   "description": "Contrition is the genuine, deep sorrow of someone who has done wrong and knows it — not the surface shame of being caught but the interior grief of having actually caused harm or broken trust. The biblical vocabulary gives this its strongest expression in the psalms of repentance: the broken and contrite heart, the crushed spirit. Contrition is the inner precondition for genuine repentance: without it, repentance is merely a change of strategy rather than a change of heart. [Covered by repentance (#135), brokenness (#18).]",
